# Generated decks. `make build` renders examples/demo.md into demo.html and the
# examples/ output, so anything annotated inside them is overwritten on the next
# build. The findings there are:
#
#   missing-integrity     - the deck template references highlight.js themes
#                           from a CDN by design; a deck is a self-contained
#                           file the author opens locally, not a served page
#                           with an origin to protect.
#   plaintext-http-link   - an http:// link to github.com in the demo content.
#
# Scanning of hotslice's own source under hotslice/ and scripts/ is unaffected.
demo.html
examples/*.html
